---
import DiagramFigure from './DiagramFigure.astro'

// Then the frameworks, and what they will not do. The agentic eval frameworks
// offer two portable metrics that run over a trace: tool correctness, a
// deterministic comparison of tools called against tools expected, which can
// gate; and task completion, judged by a model, which runs beside the gate, not
// in it. Everything else you write by hand, because ordering, preconditions,
// confirmation gates, idempotency keys, call budgets, and the execute-the-
// pending-action invariant are specific to what your agent may do and how it was
// built. A faithfulness metric is portable across every RAG system in the world.
// A "never open a ticket the customer did not ask for" assertion is portable
// across nothing. That is not a gap in your tooling, it is the work.

const general = [
  { name: 'Tool correctness', how: 'tools called vs expected', lane: 'deterministic', gate: 'gates' },
  { name: 'Task completion', how: 'did it accomplish the goal', lane: 'model judged', gate: 'tracks' },
]

const bespoke = [
  'ordering and preconditions',
  'no orphan action',
  'confirmation fidelity',
  'execute the pending action',
  'idempotency key',
  'call budget and termination',
]

const ariaLabel =
  'Two kinds of agent metric. On one side, portable framework metrics that run over any trace: tool correctness, a deterministic comparison of tools called against tools expected, which can gate; and task completion, judged by a model, which is tracked beside the gate rather than in it. On the other side, bespoke assertions portable across nothing: ordering and preconditions, no orphan action, confirmation fidelity, execute the stored pending action, the idempotency key, and call budget with termination. A faithfulness metric is portable across every RAG system; a never open a ticket assertion is portable across nothing, and writing those yourself is the work, not a workaround.'
---

<DiagramFigure label="Portable metrics, and the assertions you write yourself" ariaLabel={ariaLabel} data-ap>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
    <div>
      <span class="block font-mono text-mono-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-text-muted mb-2">
        Framework metrics · portable
      </span>
      <div class="space-y-2">
        {
          general.map((g) => (
            <div class="ap-gen rounded border border-border-dark bg-surface-container-low px-4 py-3">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                <span class="text-sm text-text-primary font-medium">{g.name}</span>
                <span class:list={['ap-gate font-mono text-mono-xs', g.gate === 'gates' ? 'is-gate' : 'is-track']}>
                  {g.gate === 'gates' ? 'gates ✓' : 'tracked'}
                </span>
              </div>
              <span class="block font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted mt-1">
                {g.how} · {g.lane}
              </span>
            </div>
          ))
        }
        <p class="m-0 pt-1 font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
          a faithfulness metric is portable across every RAG system in the world.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <span class="block font-mono text-mono-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-2">
        Bespoke assertions · portable across nothing
      </span>
      <div class="ap-bespoke rounded border px-4 py-3">
        <ul class="m-0 grid grid-cols-1 gap-1.5 p-0 list-none">
          {
            bespoke.map((b) => (
              <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-text-primary">
                <span class="ap-tick font-mono text-mono-xs shrink-0" aria-hidden="true">▸</span>
                {b}
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
        <p class="m-0 mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-border-dark font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
          a “never open a ticket the customer did not ask for” assertion is portable across nothing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="note">
    You will write more custom assertions than you did for retrieval, by a wide margin. That is not a
    gap in your tooling. It is the current state of the field, and writing those assertions yourself
    is the work, not a workaround for missing work.
  </Fragment>
</DiagramFigure>

<style is:global>
  [data-ap] .ap-gate.is-gate {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  [data-ap] .ap-gate.is-track {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  [data-ap] .ap-bespoke {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 40%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 6%, transparent);
  }
  [data-ap] .ap-tick {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }
</style>
